{
  "presses": ["L-pinky-top", "L-ring-home", "R-middle-top", "R-index-bottom"],
  "note": "T1: keys a=L-pinky-top b=L-ring-home c=R-middle-top d=R-index-bottom-in held S1={B,K,U,Y} (rot1 keys≠{a,b,c,d}). Plan: T2 press {a,b,c,x1} x1=R-index-bottom. After observe T2 symbols set S2: since x1 new, S2∩S1 size=3, missing m=S1\\S2 is sym(d) at T2 iff rot2 notice does NOT include d. If rot2 includes any of {a,b,c,d,x1}, mark those keys 'moved' (permutation unknown; no fixed points) and don’t lock/assume old placements when using set-diffs vs S1. Next planned: T3 press {a,b,d,x2} x2=R-index-home to bind sym(c) similarly (only if rot2 did not move c)."
}

{
  "presses": [
    "L-pinky-top",
    "L-ring-home",
    "R-index-bottom",
    "R-index-home"
  ],
  "note": "Have keys: A=L-pinky-top, B=L-ring-home, C=R-middle-top, D=R-index-bottom with letters set T={B,K,X,Y} (unordered, all 4 unique). T3 presses A,B,D,E where E=R-index-home. After S3 (4 symbols): T∩S3 must have size3; let m = T \\ (T∩S3) => letter on C. Let e = S3 \\ T => letter on E. Remaining 3 letters in (T∩S3) correspond to A,B,D permuted. Next pick chord to exclude one of A/B/D to pin them."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-ring-bottom", "R-pinky-top", "L-index-bottom-in", "R-middle-top"],
  "locks": {
    "L-pinky-top": "K",
    "L-ring-home": "B",
    "L-index-bottom-in": "Q",
    "R-middle-top": "Y",
    "R-index-home": "W"
  },
  "note": "T7: {L-ring-home,R-middle-top,L-index-bottom-in,R-index-home} -> {B,Q,W,Y}. Since L-index-bottom-in=Q and R-middle-top=Y => L-ring-home=B, R-index-home=W. Hence L-pinky-top=K. Rot after: L-ring-bottom <-> R-pinky-top (letters swapped, unknown each now). Next press {L-ring-bottom,R-pinky-top,L-index-bottom-in(=Q),R-middle-top(=Y)} to get their 2-letter set."
}

{
  "presses": [
    "L-middle-bottom",
    "L-pinky-top",
    "L-ring-home",
    "L-index-bottom-in"
  ],
  "note": "Add from T9: L-ring-bottom=F. T10 deduce L-middle-bottom by pressing {L-middle-bottom, L-pinky-top(K), L-ring-home(B), L-index-bottom-in(Q)}; remaining symbol => L-middle-bottom. T11 deduce R-index-top-in using {R-index-top-in, R-index-home(W), R-middle-top(Y), L-ring-bottom(F)}."
}

{
  "presses": [
    "R-index-top-in",
    "R-index-home-in",
    "R-middle-top",
    "L-ring-bottom"
  ],
  "note": "T11: press {R-index-top-in, R-index-home-in, R-middle-top, L-ring-bottom}. Use known L-ring-bottom=F; also assume R-index-home-in=W and R-middle-top=Y (per earlier). Deduce R-index-top-in as the 4th symbol (no rotation expected)."
}

{
  "presses": ["R-index-home-in", "R-middle-top", "R-index-bottom-in", "L-pinky-bottom"],
  "locks": {
    "L-pinky-home": "N",
    "R-index-home-in": "E",
    "R-middle-top": "Y",
    "R-index-bottom-in": "K"
  },
  "note": "T16 no rot: pressed {L-pinky-home,R-index-home-in,R-middle-top,R-index-bottom-in} => got {E,K,N,Y} so L-pinky-home=N; also confirms R-index-home-in=E, R-middle-top=Y, R-index-bottom-in=K. Next T17 press R-index-home-in+R-middle-top+R-index-bottom-in+L-pinky-bottom to deduce L-pinky-bottom."
}
